      {"@type":"Question","name":"Is the 30-60% India cost gap real or marketing fluff?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It's real but more nuanced than headline rates suggest. Senior US engineer rate: $120-$200/hr. Senior UK engineer rate: £90-£150/hr. Senior India studio rate: $35-$75/hr equivalent. Apply to a 4-month MVP: US/UK $90K-$200K; India studio $25K-$60K. The gap is largest on senior-led work because the senior-rate spread is largest. Mid-level and junior work shows smaller gaps. Quality parity holds for senior practitioners — the rate gap reflects cost of living, not capability."}},
      {"@type":"Question","name":"What about timezone problems?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Real but solvable. India IST is 9.5 hours ahead of EST, 12.5 hours ahead of PST, 4.5-5.5 hours ahead of GMT. Practical: 4-6 hour overlap with EST (9am-1pm EST = 6:30pm-10:30pm IST), 5-9 hour with PST. We default to your business hours for standups, weekly demos and Slack/Teams. The dev team works while you sleep — net-net, faster shipping cadence. Years of US/UK engagements running this model successfully."}},
      {"@type":"Question","name":"What about IP protection and contract enforcement?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Two layers: (1) the SOW + MSA can be governed by US state law (Delaware default) or English law for UK buyers — your choice; (2) work-for-hire IP assignment is irrevocable on milestone payment, written into every SOW, transferred to your private GitHub from day one. India's IP regime is TRIPS-compliant and respected in international courts. The actual mechanic that matters: code in your repo > legal recourse in any jurisdiction. We make sure the former is always true."}},
      {"@type":"Question","name":"Will I have communication issues?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"English fluency is native-level on every client-facing engineer at our studio (and at most senior India studios — it's table stakes). The real communication risk is asynchronous tools-of-choice mismatch (you use Slack, they use email). We default to your tools: Slack, Teams, Linear, Jira, Notion, whatever you run. Same daily-standup cadence as a co-located team."}},
      {"@type":"Question","name":"What's the quality risk vs a US/UK agency?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Quality risk on tier-1 senior India studios is comparable to tier-2 US/UK agencies and better than most offshore body-shops. The real spread is between BOUTIQUE quality vs COMMODITY quality — and both India and US/UK have boutiques and commodity shops. Pick the right boutique on either side, you get equivalent quality. The cost gap reflects market not capability. We've shipped for US Fortune 500 partners and UK FTSE 250 buyers under that quality bar."}},
      {"@type":"Question","name":"Should I do hybrid — US PM + India build team?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"This pattern (sometimes called 'on-shore + off-shore' or 'lead from home, build abroad') was big in the 2010s and is fading. Senior India studios increasingly include account-led PMs already; adding a US/UK PM layer adds 30-50% margin without adding signal. We don't recommend it unless your buyer's procurement actively requires it. Modern model: senior India studio with direct US/UK client relationship, no PM layer."}}
